# A finite fold is well-defined over an arbitrary closed, commutative, associative carrier.
forall E set,S finite_set,op fn(a,b E)E,f fn(k E)E,s E:
    S $subset E
    forall x,y E:
        op(x,y) = op(y,x)
    forall x,y,z E:
        op(op(x,y),z) = op(x,op(y,z))
    =>:
        finite_set_reduce(S,f,op,s) $in E
